WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:13.150
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.720
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.880
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.290
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.400
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.540
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.100
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.290
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.360
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.450
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.210
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.490
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:05.420
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:12.870
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:25.180
Takara Fansubs

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:33.110
<i>After surviving Alfredo's death and regaining the courage to live himself,</i>

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.640
<i>...Romeo was acclaimed as leader of the Black Brothers.</i>

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:42.610
<i>The boys presided over a solemn funeral,</i>

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:46.680
<i>...and laid their dear friend Alfredo to rest.</i>

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:55.290
Episode 31:

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:55.290
The Real Treasure

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:23.310
<i>Alfredo.</i>

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.520
<i>I'm feeling great today.</i>

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:50.900
Romeo!
- Romeo!

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.610
I wonder what's happening?

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.240
We'll find out if we watch.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:59.190
'scuse me! Comin' through!

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:29.120
A monster!

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:30.320
It's an elephant.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.390
An elephant!

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.260
Alfredo told me about those once.

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:38.300
"Elephant"?
- Yes.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:39.760
Come on, come all!

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.770
Come to see dreams and wonders!

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.770
Come to the best circus in Lombardia!

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.600
Circus!

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:48.660
Let's go!

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.780
Yes!

00:03:53.630 --> 00:04:01.640
<i>It was a sight that the boys, raised in poor villages, could only have dreamed of.</i>

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:08.210
<i>The circus cast a magic spell on their hearts.</i>

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.980
The highwire trapeze star!

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.850
What's a highwire trapeze?

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.940
It's where they walk through the sky on a wire.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.440
She's an angel.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.060
She waved at me!

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.670
No, at ME!

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.940
Welcome, children.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.000
Come in, come in!

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.620
Even we can go in?

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:44.840
Of course!

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:49.560
Ho there! First you've got to pay the entrance fee.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.920
Entrance fee?
- Two lira per person.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:53.920
Two lira... per person?

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:58.420
Country folks!
What do you expect...

00:04:58.900 --> 00:04:59.930
Anzelmo!

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:03.700
Not even knowing about the entrance fee!

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.180
Anzelmo!

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:10.320
Then how about you pay their entrance fee too, Anzelmo?

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.960
Well now, what are you doing here, dear?

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.330
I only have enough to pay for Anzelmo and me.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:21.080
And who do you think earned that money?

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:26.090
Don't get smart with me.
Pay your bar bills for once!

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:28.240
Hey, come on...

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.480
They just came collecting, and took ten lira!

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.090
Sorry, Romeo.

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:42.480
Come, come! The circus is about to start!

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:53.650
Two lira...

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.530
I'd do anything to see the circus.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.790
We might get in... if I cast a spell!

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.810
Another keepsake from your mother?

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.930
Uh-huh. She lent it to me when I left for Milan.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:18.130
She said to pray to it whenever I need help.

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:23.310
It was amazing... that time when I cried as I got soaked by the rain...

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:24.770
Yeah, okay...

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:29.410
I prayed to my mother, and the rain stopped... right then!

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:30.280
Really?

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:34.480
Pure coincidence!
Even you must know that.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:41.150
Mother, may I find two lira lying on the ground where I hit.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:42.500
Not likely.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.420
Michaelo, be careful!

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:47.920
May I find two lira.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:50.930
Watch out!

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:08.440
Bianca.

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:15.930
That's from Dr. Casella, for the logs you guys hauled for him yesterday.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:19.560
Two lira total.

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:22.090
Two lira!?

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:33.590
Looks like...

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.590
...just one person here...

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:38.490
...gets to go to the circus.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:48.840
The first one to grab that leaf gets to go to the circus.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.240
That leaf...?

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.250
Okay... I'm going to win this and go to the circus.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:57.990
Ready... get set...

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:02.230
And... go!

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:12.020
Right...!

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:19.130
Outta the way, Antonio!

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:25.640
What's the big idea?!

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.190
I'm the one going to the circus.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.290
No, me!
- Look at Romeo!

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:38.570
Just a bit further...

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.460
You okay?
- Ow.

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:57.650
I got it!

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:08.270
Everybody, calm down!

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:10.490
I should be the one who gets to go.

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:15.770
I'm the one who prayed for the two lira.

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:17.050
That was a coincidence!

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:18.960
What're you talking about?
- Wait a minute.

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:20.840
That hurt, Romeo!

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.200
That does it!

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.740
Stop! Stop, everybody!

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:30.870
You're a bunch of pre-schoolers.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:34.980
Romeo, a leader shouldn't get into fights.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.360
Oh, right...

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:41.940
That's right! These things happen if you don't act more like a leader.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.130
Can't you think of a better way?

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:48.360
Even my mother's more reliable than you!

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:49.290
What?!

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:53.680
Wait. Romeo just became the leader.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:56.940
Yeah, we have to give him a chance to get used to it.

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:59.470
Still... who's going to the circus?

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:05.180
Now I'm mad! Okay!

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:08.510
I'm the leader, so I'll do something!

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:14.040
Yes, listen to our leader.
We'll let him decide who goes.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:17.490
Fine. So no more complaints!

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:19.430
Go ahead, Romeo.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:24.630
Let Michaelo go, or else he'll cry.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:28.960
Go ahead, Romeo...
we're all friends here.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.160
We're all going.

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:36.460
It's not right for just one of the Black Brothers to go.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:39.640
I want to go to the circus with everyone.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:43.570
Of course, that'd be best, but...

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:46.160
We're all going to the circus!

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:47.910
But how?

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:51.410
We'd need 20 more lira for everybody to go.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:55.580
Right... There must be a way.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:57.470
Let's all go together.

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:18.640
It's Michaelo.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:27.300
Romeo... thought of... a way... to get... the 20 lira!

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:29.400
Please come.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:40.190
Nobody uses this wing anymore.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:43.280
I've been looking for someone to clean it up.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:45.800
Please let me do it.

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:51.390
It would really help if you can do the cleaning and repairs for 20 lira.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:52.180
But...

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:53.130
But...?

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.220
Are you sure you can do it?

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:58.130
You'd have to come during your time off.

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:02.960
Is he nuts? Clean up this dump?

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:04.360
And repair it!

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:05.520
I can do it.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.030
Very well, I'll hire you.

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:11.540
Thank you very much.

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:14.550
Don't forget to come and tell me once you're done.

00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:15.300
Yes ma'am.

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:19.500
I'll pay you then.
I'm usually in the main building.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:22.040
I hope to have it done by Tuesday morning.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:25.040
Tuesday morning?

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:26.500
Yes.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.440
This is crazy, Romeo!

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:40.480
We have to clean this whole place by Tuesday morning!

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.810
The circus is only in town until Wednesday.

00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:47.170
We'll be finished by Tuesday morning, get our twenty lira,

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:49.200
...and we can all go to the circus!

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:51.960
Easier said than done.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:04.140
Sorry, but I won't be able to help.

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:07.040
My boss won't let me work at another job.

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:11.070
Right. Neither will anybody else! We're too busy!

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:14.140
Then don't worry about it.
I'll do it by myself.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:22.920
Sure. Easy as flipping the grand cathedral on its head.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:25.360
Forget it! Forget it! Forg...!

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.720
Guess I'll have to change the floorboards, too.

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.240
Be my guest!

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.250
All right, Romeo. I'll help too.

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:40.500
Bianca!

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:48.610
<i>Beginning right then, Romeo worked every waking hour.</i>

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.570
Here, Padrone.

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:53.720
Thank you.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:57.410
I'll be going now, boss.

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:59.060
Oh, okay.

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:01.120
Don't overdo it!

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:02.590
OK!

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:26.460
Hey, Enrico!

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:28.090
Oh. Augusto.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:30.600
How's Romeo coming along?

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:36.850
They say he's working his head off.
He'll be done before sunrise.

00:14:37.090 --> 00:14:40.090
Damn... If I could only go, too...

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:53.680
It's really something.
He's not kidding around.

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:57.960
All right, I can spare ten minutes, so I'll go help out a bit.

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:02.660
Still at it?

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:06.030
You come to help too, Benalibo?

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:08.320
Just until my boss comes back at sunrise.

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:09.920
Where should I start?

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:13.430
Benalibo! Come help us in here.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:21.900
Today I'm going to surprise Romeo and get there before him.

00:15:30.770 --> 00:15:33.110
It's like a dream that's getting closer and closer to fulfillment...

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:40.790
<i>I'm going to take everyone to the circus...!</i>

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:45.110
Romeo... You're already awake?

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:49.550
Just one more push, Bianca.
Tomorrow's the day!

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:04.150
Mother, tomorrow's the day. We might all get to go to the circus!

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:11.650
I wish we could have gone together.

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:16.760
I'll tell you all about the midair trapeze when I get back.

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:18.010
Watch it!

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:23.000
Look what you've done, kid!

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:25.120
I... I'm sorry.

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:28.620
This was an expensive vase I picked up in Spain.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:32.080
C'mon, show me where Dad lives!

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:33.780
Is it in this neighborhood?

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:37.050
That boy's a chimney sweep.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.780
His father and mother live off across the mountains somewhere.

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:44.240
Say, that's pretty.

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:46.360
That's...!

00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:17.280
Oh, shoot! The second floor!

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.920
Well then, it's the appointed time.

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:23.850
I'm sorry, I haven't finished yet.

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:26.210
Could I have just a little more time?

00:17:26.260 --> 00:17:30.870
To tell you the truth, I thought you'd give up right away.

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:35.460
But now I believe that you plan on sticking to it to the end.

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:38.600
Here's the 20 lira I promised.

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.920
Michaelo!

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:57.280
We can go to the circus now.

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:01.040
We can go!

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:05.050
Michaelo!

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:14.440
What's with him?
He really wanted to go...

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:16.440
Sorry!
- Sorry!

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:24.140
It's Michaelo's.

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:27.320
How pretty! How much is this?

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:30.090
That one's expensive, ma'am.

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:34.180
Where did you get that?
You took it from Michaelo!

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:38.180
You've got nerve saying that in front of a customer!

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:40.980
Listen, I didn't want to do it either.

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:43.290
But I've got a business to run.
- What's the matter?

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:47.290
Nothing at all!

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:50.920
So that's why Michaelo...
- Then I'll take this.

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:00.690
Is everybody here?

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.860
Michaelo and Romeo aren't here yet.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:06.030
We're really going to the circus!

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:07.840
It's all thanks to Romeo.

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:09.720
I'll get to see an elephant!

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:11.120
And the midair trapeze!

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.200
Romeo!

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:20.190
We've been waiting for you. Let's leave as soon as Michaelo arrives.

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:22.220
So... where's the 20 lira?

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:26.720
I'm sorry, everybody. We're not going to the circus anymore.

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:28.720
Why not??

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:35.720
Mother, you put that necklace around my neck when I left.

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:39.460
I remember you said:

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:41.490
"You're the clumsiest one in the family, so be extra careful."

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:44.330
Well it's just like you said, Mother.

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:45.520
Don't be a crybaby, Michaelo.

00:19:47.010 --> 00:19:48.240
You're a Black Brother.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:50.990
But I thought you were...

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:54.080
We can go another time.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.680
Romeo, how did you get this?

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:11.330
Dished out the 22 lira, before he even noticed!

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:13.180
What a madcap.

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:17.020
But we all agreed with our leader.

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:17.560
Yep.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:22.080
We remember our mothers and fathers too...

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:24.570
...so we all feel exactly the same as you.

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:30.570
Are you sure you don't mind?
You all really wanted to go.

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:33.700
This necklace is far more important.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:40.960
There he goes again.
What a crybaby.

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:46.510
No! No...
I'm crying because I'm so happy.

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:56.560
Thank you, Romeo... everybody.

00:20:57.200 --> 00:20:59.320
Romeo really is our leader.

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:01.310
He's a wonderful leader.

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:02.600
Yeah.

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:11.550
Say, Romeo... For the rest of the day,

00:21:11.550 --> 00:21:13.560
...why don't we swap stories about our home towns?

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:16.880
Good idea. Let's.

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:18.590
Don't forget about our mothers!

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:32.090
<i>The boys had friends they could laugh and cry with,</i>

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:38.080
<i>...and they knew that was better than any treasure.</i>

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:44.490
<i>They enjoyed that day from the bottom of their hearts.</i>

00:21:55.340 --> 00:21:56.680
<i>To show my gratitude to Dr. Casella,</i>

00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:59.080
<i>...who cared so kindly for me when I broke my leg...</i>

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:04.240
<i>Bianca and I decided to put on a puppet show for him.</i>

00:22:05.610 --> 00:22:08.070
<i>Once upon a time...</i>

00:22:08.650 --> 00:22:11.840
See you then!

00:22:08.650 --> 00:22:11.840
<i>A Lovely Christmas Eve</i>

00:22:08.650 --> 00:22:11.840
Next time:

00:22:13.250 --> 00:22:17.250
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:29.960
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:34.260
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:38.460
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:38.660 --> 00:22:42.660
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:47.570
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:47.570 --> 00:22:51.470
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:51.870 --> 00:22:58.770
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:23:00.470 --> 00:23:04.370
